      "claim": "In situ rat brain perfusion showed the ketoprofen-glucose prodrug crossed the BBB with a brain uptake of 1.33 pmol/mg/min and was labeled permeable with transporter-mediated transport.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "In vivo rat brain concentration of a glucose-bearing compound was 3.1 nmol/g, with transport possibly aided by GLUT1, demonstrating systemic BBB passage.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "Brain microdialysis in SD rats after intravenous dosing showed rapid BBB crossing with an unbound brain Cmax of 0.16 µg/mL, providing direct evidence of meaningful CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple direct in-vivo and perfusion records demonstrate meaningful BBB penetration after systemic administration, with no contradictory direct CNS-access evidence. The disrupted-barrier query condition further supports a pass prediction.",
